  "notes": "Native script supplied only 0-30 and round tens + 100 (સો); compound native spellings (31-99) are OMITTED pending verification rather than guessed — romanized forms (source-verified) cover the full 0-100. Roman normalized to ASCII. Fractions are cognate with Hindi usage (dodh=1.5, adhee=2.5, savaa=1.25 e.g. સવા સો = 125, pona=3/4 of next unit e.g. પોણા બેસો = 175, saada=+1/2 e.g. સાડા ત્રણસો = 350). Verify with a native speaker. Indian numbering uses lakh/karod."
